# Browser
# Mobilize does not say what its Warriors attack (CR 702.181a), so as each enters attacking its controller chooses a player,
# planeswalker or battle for it (CR 508.4), not necessarily what the creature with mobilize attacks. Voice of Victory attacks
# Bot2 on turn 3 while Bot2 has Liliana of the Veil (loyalty 3); Bot1 sends one Warrior at Liliana and the other at Bot2.
# Voice (1 power) and a Warrior take Bot2 to 18, the other Warrior takes Liliana to 2. In the browser the question is a
# choice, not a target, and says what it is for; the page then stands each Warrior in its own combat group.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Voice of Victory
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Liliana of the Veil
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Voice of Victory.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot2.Hand.Liliana of the Veil.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Voice of Victory > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Choice for Voice of Victory
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = Choose what it attacks as it enters attacking: a player, a planeswalker or a battle.  ·  2 possible choices
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
? Combat.Attackers = Voice of Victory > Bot2; Warrior Token > Liliana of the Veil; Warrior Token > Bot2
? Client.Bot1.Combat = Attacking Bot2: Voice of Victory, Warrior Token; Attacking Liliana of the Veil: Warrior Token
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
